From 1581c288bfeeace122bb7e2462726e4c449e86ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bmh129 <11478682+bmh129@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:44:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Linux: resize and move the window again right after a
 resize or move

BeginResize and StartDrag hand the pointer to the desktop, and the
compositor keeps the button's release (it grabs the pointer on Wayland).
egui then still thought the button held, so the next press on an edge or
the title bar didn't start another resize or move until a click inside the
window released it. window_controls::desktop_grab now notes the hand-over,
and the raw input hook adds the primary button's release to the next
input, once, unless that input brings one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
